<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 29,697,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 29,697,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 01/22/97    01/15/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 29,697,000  30,061,000    26,851,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	 144,984     265,796	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	34,948,000  34,948,000    33,569,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,140,728  27,730,360	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   01/22/97    01/15/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   5,116,000   5,420,000     4,678,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    5,034,000   4,837,000     4,371,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  4,922,000   5,103,000     4,713,000</p>
<p> South Central    3,223,000   3,196,000     2,824,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  4,135,000   4,058,000     3,441,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,188,000   5,259,000     4,952,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  2,077,000   2,187,000     1,872,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	29,697,000  30,061,000    26,851,000</p>
